{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D98nNL2ZXb7PShKRA4kVQW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# SPEC v1 — Todo List CLI MVP\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tA single-binary CLI todo list, grown milestone by milestone so `just check` is green from the first commit. Domain logic is a pure core over `List[Todo]`; Cats Effect sits at the edge for the filesystem and stdout. The store is one YAML file. The same data is reachable two ways directly from the CLI: a colored, aligned table for a human at a terminal, and raw YAML for a script or another tool.\n6\t\n7\t## Scope\n8\t\n9\t- One user, one machine, one YAML file as the store.\n10\t- Commands: `add`, `list`, `done`, `edit`, `remove`.\n11\t- Two renderers for `list`: a colored table (default) and YAML.\n12\t- A CI workflow that runs the same `just check` gate on every push and PR.\n13\t\n14\t## Non-goals (later specs)\n15\t\n16\t- Config files or environment-variable precedence for defaults.\n17\t- Filtering, sorting, priorities, due dates or tags.\n18\t- Any store other than a local YAML file (no SQLite, no remote/S3).\n19\t\n20\t## Architecture sketch"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b2ec4d8-2a9f-499e-9187-8f4707e1313e","uuid":"8e8039d0-3ca6-48ac-a0e3-42edbc56e65e","timestamp":"2026-09-29T22:01:13.654Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/isaiasbartelborth/Projects/hivemind/todo-list-cli/develop/docs/specs/SPEC.v1-todo-list-cli-mvp.md","content":"# SPEC v1 — Todo List CLI MVP\n\n## Goal\n\nA single-binary CLI todo list, grown milestone by milestone so `just check` is green from the first commit. Domain logic is a pure core over `List[Todo]`; Cats Effect sits at the edge for the filesystem and stdout. The store is one YAML file. The same data is reachable two ways directly from the CLI: a colored, aligned table for a human at a terminal, and raw YAML for a script or another tool.\n\n## Scope\n\n- One user, one machine, one YAML file as the store.\n- Commands: `add`, `list`, `done`, `edit`, `remove`.\n- Two renderers for `list`: a colored table (default) and YAML.\n- A CI workflow that runs the same `just check` gate on every push and PR.\n\n## Non-goals (later specs)\n\n- Config files or environment-variable precedence for defaults.\n- Filtering, sorting, priorities, due dates or tags.\n- Any store other than a local YAML file (no SQLite, no remote/S3).\n\n## Architecture sketch","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":131}}}
